//medium.com/@vankudoth.hemanth.mec22",x:"https://x.com/VHemanthNaik",huggingface:"https://huggingface.co/Hemanth451"},writingBlurb:"Explainers on sequence models and MLOps on Medium, and hands-on Kaggle notebooks on the tools I reach for with tabular data: gradient boosting, hyperparameter search and explainability.",contactBlurb:"I’m a data scientist at PlayVision, and always up for a hard problem — a model that has to survive production, an agent that has to stop guessing, or a dataset nobody has made sense of yet. If that sounds like something you’re working on, say hi."},Js=[{id:"init",t:0,curve:"train",when:"Jul 2022",text:"Init: mechanical engineering, IIT (BHU)",x:100,y:0,w:300,from:[96,26],bend:-.35},{id:"overfit",t:.36,curve:"val",when:"2024",text:"Overfit to tutorials. Briefly.",x:272,y:52,w:170,from:[268,80],bend:.35},{id:"writing",t:Su(2024.72),curve:"train",when:"Sep 2024",text:"Wrote about GRUs, LSTMs & MLOps",x:116,y:236,w:170,from:[262,232],bend:-.3},{id:"job",t:1,curve:"train",when:"Now",text:"Data scientist at PlayVision",x:404,y:136,w:176,from:[530,182],bend:-.25},{id:"ocr",t:Su(2026.42),curve:"train",when:"Jun 2026",text:"OCR pipeline: CER 0.355 → 0.072",x:290,y:286,w:180,from:[452,286],bend:-.35}],ej=[{org:"PlayVision",role:"Data Scientist",when:"2026 — now",status:"serving"},{org:"BaseRock AI",role:"Intern",sub:"Agentic QA & testing",when:"2025",status:"completed",href:"https://www.baserock.ai"}],ju=[{anchor:"herdr",repo:"VHemanth45/herdr_agents_tracker",title:"Herdr Agents Tracker",domain:"Agent tooling · open source",year:"2026",summary:"A plugin for Herdr, the runtime coding agents live on, that answers what every heavy Claude Code and Codex user wants to know: will I hit my limit before it resets — and which agent is burning through it?",spec:[["Problem","Usage trackers say “52% used”. That doesn’t tell you whether you’ll make it to the reset, or which of five running agents is eating the window."],["Approach","It asks Claude Code and Codex for their own numbers — no credentials, no prompts, no telemetry — and forecasts from the last hour of work, so a sudden burst shows up at once: “52% (100% in 1h40m)”. Every agent gets a context meter and its share of the limit; alerts fire at 80% and 95%, and again when the limit resets."],["Engineering","Python’s standard library only — zero dependencies. 129 tests in CI on macOS and Ubuntu × Python 3.11–3.14, and a CLI with JSON output and exit codes for scripts."]],stack:["Python (stdlib only)","Herdr plugin","Claude Code","Codex","GitHub Actions"],figure:{type:"herdr",src:`${qs}img/herdr.webp`,alt:"Herdr terminal window showing Claude and Codex usage limits with progress bars, token activity and a daily activity heatmap",width:1440,height:850},caption:"Live: the two agents on this page, tracked the way the plugin tracks yours. “Screenshot” is the real thing.",links:[{label:"Source",href:`${q}/herdr_agents_tracker`},{label:"Install",href:`${q}/herdr_agents_tracker#install`}],note:"★ 4 on GitHub · MIT licensed",herd:{claude:"Hey — that’s us!",codex:"That’s my usage bar."}},{repo:"VHemanth45/OCR",title:"RenAIssance OCR",domain:"Document AI",year:"2026",summary:"OCR for historical printed documents — old typefaces, uneven ink and archaic spelling, exactly where off-the-shelf OCR falls apart.",spec:[["Problem","The Tesseract baseline gets about one character in three wrong (CER 0.355)."],["Approach","A fine-tuned YOLOv8n finds the main text block, lines are segmented and aligned to ground truth, then recognisers are compared one rung at a time: Tesseract, fine-tuned TrOCR, a Kraken CRNN — with Gemini 2.5 Flash as a post-correction pass."],["Result","CER 0.355 → 0.072 and WER 0.771 → 0.236 on 296 validation lines: 80% fewer character errors than the baseline."]],stack:["PyTorch","YOLOv8","TrOCR","Kraken","Tesseract","Gemini 2.5 Flash"],figure:{type:"bars",max:.8,ticks:[0,.2,.4,.6,.8],groups:[{label:"Tesseract",sub:"Baseline"},{label:"TrOCR",sub:"Fine-tuned"},{label:"Kraken",sub:"CRNN"},{label:"CRNN + LLM",sub:"Post-correct"}],series:[{name:"CER",color:"#1f77b4",values:[.3553,.175,.0928,.0724]},{name:"WER",color:"#ff7f0e",values:[.7713,.4657,.3335,.2363]}],note:"−80% CER vs. the baseline"},caption:"Error rates by pipeline stage, 296 validation lines. Lower is better.",links:[{label:"Source",href:`${q}/OCR`}],herd:{codex:"Checking the CER math…"}},{repo:"VHemanth45/risk_agent",title:"ScamShield",domain:"Multimodal agents",year:"2026",summary:"A multimodal scam detector behind a FastAPI service: send screenshots, voice notes and chat logs, get back a risk score, the evidence behind it, and what to do next.",spec:[["Problem","Pig-butchering chats, fake exchange dashboards and tech-support calls arrive as images and audio — a text-only filter misses most of them."],["Approach","Screenshots are embedded with CLIP and matched against a labelled “scam genome” in Qdrant, and read with EasyOCR; voice notes go through Whisper. All the evidence is embedded with bge-base and retrieved top-5, alongside a per-user memory, before an LLM returns a strict-JSON verdict."],["Data","~800 labelled dialogues, 1,280 rows of a public scam-conversation set, and 119 labelled screenshots across 12 scam and legit categories."]],stack:["FastAPI","Qdrant","CLIP","bge-base","EasyOCR","Whisper","Gemini / Llama 3.3"],figure:{type:"image",src:`${qs}img/risk-agent.webp`,alt:"ScamShield command-line client showing a LOW risk verdict (1%) for a chat log, a table of retrieved evidence with similarity scores, and recommended actions",width:1600,height:836},caption:"A real run: a harmless chat log scores 1% risk, with the retrieved evidence to back it up.",links:[{label:"Source",href:`${q}/risk_agent`}],note:"Built with @anjaliii255"},{repo:"VHemanth45/BestHire",title:"BestHire",domain:"Retrieval & ranking",year:"2026",summary:"A candidate-ranking engine for the Redrob hackathon: it reads a job description, ranks the applicant pool, and catches the fake “honeypot” profiles planted in it.",spec:[["Approach","Hard gates and honeypot checks first; then section-weighted job-description embeddings (bge-small), a cross-encoder rerank of the top 200, and structured signals — each min-max normalised and blended 35 / 45 / 20."],["Engineering","Fully deterministic — pinned reference date, ID tie-breaks — and ranks offline in under 5 seconds on a CPU."],["Demo","200 sample candidates in, 193 through the hard gates, zero honeypots in the top 100."]],stack:["sentence-transformers","bge-small","bge-reranker","Gradio","Hugging Face Spaces"],figure:{type:"image",src:`${qs}img/besthire.webp`,alt:"BestHire running on Hugging Face Spaces, with sliders for cross-encoder, semantic and structured weights and buttons to rank a sample or an uploaded file",width:1600,height:656},caption:"Live on Hugging Face Spaces. The three sliders are the three stages.",links:[{label:"Live demo",href:"https://huggingface.co/spaces/Hemanth451/BestHire_Team_Errors"},{label:"Source",href:`${q}/BestHire`}],note:"Team Errors, with @anjaliii255"}],tj=[{title:"Echo",kind:"macOS app",year:"2026",summary:"Select text anywhere, press ⌃⌥E, and Echo rewrites it in your own voice — learned from 3–10 of your writing samples — without changing the facts. Runs on a local Llama 3 via Ollama, or Claude with your own key.",facts:["v1.1.1","Swift · no third-party deps","AES-GCM profiles, key in Keychain","Universal binary via CI"],figure:{type:"echo",before:"Hi team, I wanted to let you know that we will be moving the review to next week because we need some more time to get the details right.",after:"Hi team — we’re moving the review to next week so we can get the details right."},caption:"Same facts, fewer words, your tone.",links:[{label:"Download",href:`${q}/Echo/releases/latest`},{label:"Source",href:`${q}/Echo`}]}],Yh=["#1f77b4","#ff7f0e","#2ca02c","#d62728","#9467bd","#8c564b","#e377c2","#7f7f7f","#bcbd22","#17becf"],nj=[{id:"all",label:"All"},{id:"ml",label:"ML & eval"},{id:"l